IMPORT prelude

-- Medical (Therapy, Education and Research) Act 1972 (Singapore) -- giving one's own body (ss 3, 8, 9), gifts by relatives in the
-- order of the Schedule (s 4), when a donee must refuse (s 5), who may be a donee and for what (s 7), unspecified donees (s 10),
-- unclaimed bodies (ss 12, 15), authorising a post-mortem (ss 13, 14), when removal is lawful (s 16) and the Coroner's power (s 17).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (page footer "version in force from 1/5/2023"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MTERA1972.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021
-- and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The latest amending Act in its Legislative History is Act 11 of 2023 (Healthcare
-- Services (Amendment) Act 2023, commenced 1 May 2023), annotated against s 2, s 2A, s 12 and s 15. Section numbers follow the body:
-- the arrangement at the top of the deposit is out of step (it numbers "Short title" as nothing and "Appointment of designated
-- officers" as 1).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0184 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For a person the answer is: whether and how they can give their body or authorise a post-mortem, and what
-- their family can do after their death. The Act has 17 sections and one Schedule, so almost all of it is encoded. Not encoded: the
-- short title, the definitions beyond their effect, the appointment of designated officers (s 2A) and the gazetting of approved
-- institutions (s 2B), the medical examination authorised by a gift (s 6), the donee's duty not to mutilate and the custody of the
-- remainder (s 11(2), (3)), and the Coroners Act 2010 and Interpretation Act 1965 provisions that s 16 refers to (not read here).
-- The Act creates no offence and no penalty.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Medical (Therapy, Education and Research) Act 1972 -- bodies`

DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `medical or dental education`
    `research`
    `advancement of medical or dental science`
    `therapy`
    `transplantation`
    `commercial sale`

DECLARE Donee IS ONE OF
    `an approved hospital`
    `an approved medical or dental school, college or university`
    `a specified individual`
    `an unapproved private institution`

DECLARE Moment IS ONE OF
    `well before death`
    `immediately before death`
    `after death`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is an institutional purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `commercial sale` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `7 -- who may be a donee, and for what`

-- s 7: "The following persons may become donees ... for the purposes stated: (a) any approved hospital for medical or dental
-- education, research, advancement of medical or dental science, therapy or transplantation; (b) any approved medical or dental
-- school, college or university for [the same purposes]; (c) any specified individual for therapy or transplantation needed by the
-- individual." An institution is "approved" only by Gazette notification under s 2B.
GIVEN `the donee` IS A Donee, `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `needed by that individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donee may receive the gift for the purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the donee`
    WHEN `an approved hospital` THEN `the purpose is an institutional purpose` `the purpose`
    WHEN `an approved medical or dental school, college or university` THEN `the purpose is an institutional purpose` `the purpose`
    WHEN `a specified individual` THEN
            `needed by that individual`
        AND CONSIDER `the purpose`
            WHEN `therapy` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `transplantation` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 and 8 -- giving one's own body`

-- s 3: "Any person who is not mentally disordered and who is 18 years of age or above may give all or any part of his or her body
-- for any of the purposes specified in section 7, the gift to take effect upon death."
-- s 8: a s 3 gift "may be made by the donor either in writing at any time or orally in the presence of 2 or more witnesses during a
-- last illness".
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `is mentally disordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may give his or her body` IF
    `age in years` >= 18 AND (NOT `is mentally disordered`)

GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `witnesses present` IS A NUMBER, `during a last illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form is one the Act allows` IF
        `in writing`
    OR  (`witnesses present` >= 2 AND `during a last illness`)

GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `is mentally disordered` IS A BOOLEAN, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `witnesses present` IS A NUMBER,
      `during a last illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donor's gift is validly made` IF
        `the person may give his or her body` `age in years` `is mentally disordered`
    AND `the form is one the Act allows` `in writing` `witnesses present` `during a last illness`

§§ `9 -- revoking a gift`

-- s 9: a gift "may be revoked by the donor at any time -- (a) by a signed statement in writing delivered to the donee; (b) by an oral
-- statement made in the presence of 2 or more persons and communicated to the donee; or (c) by a written document to that effect
-- found on his or her person or in his or her effects."
GIVEN `signed statement delivered to the donee` IS A BOOLEAN, `persons present at an oral statement` IS A NUMBER,
      `oral statement communicated to the donee` IS A BOOLEAN, `revoking document found on the person or in the effects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gift is revoked` IF
        `signed statement delivered to the donee`
    OR  (`persons present at an oral statement` >= 2 AND `oral statement communicated to the donee`)
    OR  `revoking document found on the person or in the effects`

§§ `Schedule, 4 and 14 -- relatives, in order of priority`

-- The Schedule (for ss 4(1) and 14(1)): "1. The spouse 2. An adult son or daughter 3. Either parent 4. An adult brother or sister
-- 5. A guardian of the deceased person at the time of the deceased person's death 6. Any person authorised or under obligation to
-- dispose of the body of the deceased person". A minor child or sibling and a friend are not listed (rank 0 here).
DECLARE Relative IS ONE OF
    `the spouse`
    `an adult son or daughter`
    `a parent`
    `an adult brother or sister`
    `the guardian at the time of death`
    `a person obliged to dispose of the body`
    `a minor son or daughter`
    `a friend`

GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule rank` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relative`
    WHEN `the spouse` THEN 1
    WHEN `an adult son or daughter` THEN 2
    WHEN `a parent` THEN 3
    WHEN `an adult brother or sister` THEN 4
    WHEN `the guardian at the time of death` THEN 5
    WHEN `a person obliged to dispose of the body` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 4(1) (gift) and s 14(1) (post-mortem) use the same words: a person in the Schedule, "in the order of priority stated, when
-- persons in prior classes are not available at the time of death, and in the absence of actual notice of contrary indications by
-- the deceased person, or actual notice of opposition of a member of the same class or a prior class". ss 4(2), 14(2): "after death
-- or immediately before death". Opposition from a LATER class does not stand in the way.
-- `the most senior class available` is the class of highest priority with someone available at the time of death.
GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative, `the most senior class available` IS A Relative, `when it is done` IS A Moment,
      `actual notice of the deceased's contrary indication` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `actual notice of opposition from the same or a prior class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relative may act for the deceased` IF
        `the Schedule rank` `the relative` > 0
    AND `the Schedule rank` `the relative` <= `the Schedule rank` `the most senior class available`
    AND (NOT `actual notice of the deceased's contrary indication`)
    AND (NOT `actual notice of opposition from the same or a prior class`)
    AND CONSIDER `when it is done`
        WHEN `well before death` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5 -- when the donee must refuse`

-- s 5: the donee "must not accept the gift if the donee has actual notice of contrary indications by the deceased person or that a
-- gift by a member of a class is opposed by a member of the same class or a prior class."
GIVEN `actual notice of the deceased's contrary indication` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `actual notice of opposition from the same or a prior class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donee must not accept` IF
    `actual notice of the deceased's contrary indication` OR `actual notice of opposition from the same or a prior class`

§§ `10 -- a gift with no named donee`

-- s 10(1): a gift "may be made to a specified donee or without specifying a donee". (2) If no donee is specified, "the designated
-- officer of the approved hospital in which the death ... has taken place or to which the body ... has been removed may accept the
-- gift as donee upon or following the death for the purposes of section 7(a) or (b)". So an unnamed gift cannot go to an individual.
GIVEN `died in or was removed to that approved hospital` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the designated officer may accept an unnamed gift` IF
    `died in or was removed to that approved hospital` AND `the purpose is an institutional purpose` `the purpose`

§§ `12 and 15 -- unclaimed bodies`

-- s 12 (use) and s 15 (post-mortem): where the body "has not been claimed from an approved hospital or from an institution
-- maintained on public funds, for more than 24 hours after death, the Director-General may authorise in writing" its use for the
-- s 7 purposes (s 12) or its post-mortem examination (s 15). Exactly 24 hours is not "more than 24 hours".
GIVEN `hours unclaimed since death` IS A NUMBER, `held by an approved hospital or a publicly funded institution` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may authorise use of the unclaimed body` IF
        `hours unclaimed since death` > 24
    AND `held by an approved hospital or a publicly funded institution`
    AND `authorised in writing`

§§ `13 -- authorising one's own post-mortem`

-- s 13(1): any person "not mentally disordered and ... 18 years of age or above may either in writing at any time or orally in the
-- presence of 2 or more witnesses during his or her last illness authorise the post-mortem examination of his or her body for the
-- purpose of establishing or confirming the cause of death or of investigating the existence or nature of abnormal conditions."
-- (2) effective upon death. The same capacity and form as a gift under ss 3 and 8.
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `is mentally disordered` IS A BOOLEAN, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `witnesses present` IS A NUMBER,
      `during a last illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person's post-mortem authority is valid` IF
    `the donor's gift is validly made` `age in years` `is mentally disordered` `in writing` `witnesses present` `during a last illness`

§§ `16 and 17 -- when removal or post-mortem is lawful`

-- s 16(1): removal and use "in accordance with section 3, 4 or 12" or a post-mortem "in accordance with the provisions of Part 3"
-- "is lawful". (2) But none may be effected except "(a) by a registered medical practitioner, who must have satisfied himself or
-- herself that the death ... has been determined and certified in accordance with section 2A of the Interpretation Act 1965; or
-- (b) where the Coroner has ordered the release of the body under section 22(3)(c) of the Coroners Act 2010, in a case where an
-- inquiry is to be held". Read literally, limb (b) does not say who performs the removal.
-- s 17: ss 3, 4, 13, 14 and 15 "do not affect the authority of the Coroner to direct the post-mortem examination".
DECLARE Basis IS ONE OF
    `the donor's own gift`
    `a relative's gift`
    `the Director-General's authorisation for an unclaimed body`
    `a post-mortem authorised under Part 3`
    `no authority under the Act`

GIVEN `the basis` IS A Basis, `by a registered medical practitioner satisfied the death was certified` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Coroner ordered release of the body for an inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the removal or post-mortem is lawful` IF
        CONSIDER `the basis`
        WHEN `no authority under the Act` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    AND (`by a registered medical practitioner satisfied the death was certified` OR `the Coroner ordered release of the body for an inquiry`)

GIVEN `the family objects` IS A BOOLEAN, `the deceased objected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act stops a Coroner-directed post-mortem` IF
    FALSE
